WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.450
- I saw our next guest

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:05.120
at a George Strait concert
this summer, and just wow.

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:06.690
Her voice, incredible.

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:07.900
The performance was incredible.

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:09.040
I was so floored.

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:11.710
She was one of Rolling Stones
10 new artists to know.

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:13.180
I did not know that at the time.

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:14.780
And she's here today

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:16.830
with a performance of her latest single,

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:20.170
it's called, "I Can't" and it's
off her album, "Supernova,"

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:21.900
but why don't we chat with her first?

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:24.152
Everybody, please say
hello to Caitlyn Smith.

00:00:24.152 --> 00:00:29.152
(audience applauding)
(upbeat music)

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:30.674
Oh, my gosh.

00:00:30.674 --> 00:00:33.580
I'm so excited that you're on my show.

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:34.910
I literally was so floored.

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:35.743
I was so excited.

00:00:35.743 --> 00:00:36.576
I hadn't seen a show.

00:00:36.576 --> 00:00:39.210
I hadn't seen a live concert
in four years that night

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:42.070
and I was so excited to see George.

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:44.340
And then I ended up
being so floored by you.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:45.330
I don't know if you saw my tweet,

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:47.380
but I was like, you're incredible.

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.143
Just great job. Well done.
- Thank you.

00:00:49.143 --> 00:00:50.947
(Caitlyn laughs)

00:00:50.947 --> 00:00:51.780
Thank you so much.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:52.620
I probably didn't know
when you were there,

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:54.010
I probably just would've peed my pants

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:55.050
when I got on the stage.
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:56.040
So thank you.

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:57.080
That means the world.

00:00:57.080 --> 00:00:59.970
And wow, that show was so much fun.

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:02.370
Seeing the king of country music.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:03.203
Incredible.
- Oh, my god.

00:01:03.203 --> 00:01:04.610
How did you end up touring with him?

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:05.520
You're touring.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:06.690
That's amazing.

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:07.523
- It was incredible.

00:01:07.523 --> 00:01:08.660
Well, a handful of years ago,

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:10.860
I was out on the road with
Tim McGraw and Faith Hill

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:12.400
on their Soul2Soul tour.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:15.290
And they have the same
promoter as George Strait.

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:18.380
So the promoter was walking
around during our soundcheck

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:21.450
and he heard us play and he was like,

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:22.860
we gotta get her on the George show.

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:25.920
So thanks to that guy.
- [Kelly] Oh, my God.

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:29.040
- We did a show at
Gillette Stadium in Boston

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.550
with George in 2019.

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:35.230
And he actually watched
us play side stage.

00:01:35.230 --> 00:01:38.590
And so, not only am I
playing my first stadium,

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:41.180
but I see the king of country,

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:43.230
like in my peripheral vision
the whole show, I'm like,

00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:44.900
aah, this is crazy.

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:46.580
- Oh my gosh.
- And then he asked us to do

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:47.780
a bunch of shows after that,

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:48.826
which was so cool.

00:01:48.826 --> 00:01:49.659
(Caitlyn chuckles)

00:01:49.659 --> 00:01:53.140
- George Strait was side
stage just watching your show?

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:55.080
You have peaked and it's amazing.

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:56.440
That is amazing.

00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:57.480
Oh my God.

00:01:57.480 --> 00:01:58.313
I would freak out.

00:01:58.313 --> 00:01:59.430
I don't know if I'd like that.
(audience applauding)

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:00.730
I think I'd be so nervous.

00:02:01.570 --> 00:02:02.810
I would've been terrified.

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:04.880
Well, what's been your favorite moment,

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:05.713
like touring with him?

00:02:05.713 --> 00:02:07.460
I gotta say that picture
was pretty awesome.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:08.630
Was that Vince Vaughn?

00:02:08.630 --> 00:02:10.910
- Yeah. That was so random.

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:12.730
That was definitely one
of my favorite moments

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:14.830
of doing these shows is randomly,

00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:17.330
he does these shots between his Encore,

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:19.190
which he gets some friends
together in the back

00:02:19.190 --> 00:02:21.210
and then Vince Vaughn
was just chilling there,

00:02:21.210 --> 00:02:23.900
so I got to chat with him.

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:25.230
Well, what is life?

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:26.530
That was so random. (laughs)

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:28.630
- Oh my gosh. I love
how texaneers is like,

00:02:28.630 --> 00:02:29.630
we're just gonna do this shot

00:02:29.630 --> 00:02:31.111
and I'm gonna get back
out there and kill it.

00:02:31.111 --> 00:02:33.080
(audience laugh)
I love George Strait so much.

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:34.090
- It was awesome.

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:36.140
- Oh, well, your voice is incredible,

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:37.490
but this is a really cool thing

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:39.440
I wanted to make sure everybody knew.

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:42.770
You founded a collective
called Girls of Nashville.

00:02:42.770 --> 00:02:44.550
Tell everybody what that's about.

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:45.680
- Yes.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:48.910
So Girls of Nashville is a show

00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:52.800
that we put on four times a
year in Nashville, Tennessee,

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:56.850
and it's really just a
little showcase of women

00:02:56.850 --> 00:02:58.840
that we think are awesome.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:02.210
We've had incredible artists
join us like Kacey Musgraves,

00:03:02.210 --> 00:03:03.043
Maren Morris,

00:03:03.043 --> 00:03:05.800
but, you know, we also
keep our ear to the ground

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:08.450
and kind of pull up
young acts that we think,

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:10.720
man, they should get a record
deal or a publishing deal

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:14.720
and love to shine a spotlight
on young women as well.

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:19.720
And so it's this growing
little community that I love.

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:21.030
It's near and dear to my heart.

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:22.160
- I think that's so cool.

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:22.993
You're paying it forward.

00:03:22.993 --> 00:03:23.826
And I gotta say,

00:03:23.826 --> 00:03:25.410
I think we're meant to be
friends because all of a sudden

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:26.910
you've just announced to all Texas people

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:29.300
that you like to be around
George, Kacey, Maren.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:30.270
We're all Texans.
(audience applaud)

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:31.183
I'm just saying.

00:03:32.177 --> 00:03:34.100
I think we're meant to be friends.

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:36.160
- I Should have maybe been born in Texas.

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:38.280
I love Texas.
(Kelly chuckles)

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.360
- Well, you're gonna be
performing, "I Can't,"

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:41.193
after the break.

00:03:41.193 --> 00:03:42.610
So what's this song about?

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:43.443
- Yeah.

00:03:43.443 --> 00:03:46.890
So this song is about living in Nashville,

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:48.330
you know, for the last decade.

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:50.710
And you know, I'm a totally
different person now

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:51.880
than when I moved there,

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:53.310
and so is the city.

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:55.390
Like, I don't know if you
were there 10 years ago,

00:03:55.390 --> 00:03:57.410
but it has changed completely.

00:03:57.410 --> 00:04:00.599
- I was there 10 Years ago
- And the song just,

00:04:00.599 --> 00:04:01.690
Yeah.
- It's crazy different.

00:04:01.690 --> 00:04:03.880
There's like 88 people a
day that move there now.

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:04.950
It's crazy.

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:05.990
- It's insane.

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:07.856
Bachelorette capital of the world.

00:04:07.856 --> 00:04:08.809
(Kelly laughs)

00:04:08.809 --> 00:04:11.590
But I was driving by downtown
and seeing all the cranes

00:04:11.590 --> 00:04:12.886
and all the skyscrapers,

00:04:12.886 --> 00:04:16.190
and the idea of this song
hit me of like, you know,

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:17.570
this ain't a 20 minute town no more

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:18.530
don't look the same,

00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:21.360
like, that's where the first
lines of the song came from.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:24.190
And I realized that change
is something in our life

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:26.270
that is inevitable,

00:04:26.270 --> 00:04:28.130
but it is not easy.

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:30.530
You know, when we come up
to those things that's like,

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:32.830
we need to let someone go, something go,

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:34.610
things that we need to
fix inside ourselves,

00:04:34.610 --> 00:04:37.290
it can be so hard and you
can feel like you just can't.

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:39.530
And so I recorded this song.

00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:41.980
A big thank you to my friends Old Dominion

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:43.170
for hopping on it.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:44.230
- Casual.

00:04:44.230 --> 00:04:45.530
- I love it.
(audience applaud)

00:04:45.530 --> 00:04:47.350
- So fun. (laughs)

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:49.940
- I know about Old Dominion
because of Shane McAnally.

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:52.450
My friend, Shane, he works
with them a lot, but yeah.

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:53.460
I'm so mad at him

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:54.900
that we never had a
conversation about you.

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:56.800
I'm gonna take that up with him later.

